The problem with signed policies (in my opinion) is that they cannot
reflect change.  I believe that computing policy requires a certain
degree of flexibility; no policy can cover every situation, and the
advances in technology (or the lessening of its cost) can make even
the best policies obsolete within months of their creation.

What do you do when the policy changes?  Contact all XXXX users and
get them to sign a new form?  I think not.  Signatures on policy
