It's not the morals *I* worry about, as a system administrator, it's
  
  1) the copyright violations, especially in those groups whose
     purpose is defined in the List of Groups as "copyright
     violations"
  
  2) The load on our machine, both from the enormous amount of space
     used by the binaries/pictures groups (about 1/5 of the WHOLE
     feed) and by the dialup traffic caused by everyone downloading 
     their pictures to their PC's at night (on our site this is
     sometimes crippling, since we have a shortage of dialup lines)
 
  3) to a lesser extent, the risk that some politician will make a
     stink and cost us access to all of the groups not directly
     related to our work. Ditto the possibility of the "PC-Police"
     within our institution.

We carry the pictures groups right now but I am about to propose that
we get rid of them. I don't think the benefit outweighs the hassle.
Anyone with a modem who wants access to these things (and you need
a modem to download and view the pictures here since most users don't
have access to anything but ascii terminals) can get them free from
any of dozens of local bulletin boards. I don't think we're obligated
to carry them any more than the library is *obligated* to carry
Hustler, which they are not.

Disclaimer: this isn't policy, formal or informal, this is just my
current personal leaning after a long discussion about these groups on
news.admin.policy

thanks, Betsy



