building, and for whatever reason the security people really took it
seriously (the one time I have seen a University bomb threat taken
seriously resulted in the building being sealed for over 12 hours
while they searched the place).  In this case, I would consider it
reasonable for the investigators to conduct a detailed search of the
building to locate the bomb.  Suppose they found some evidence of a
crime in somebody's office desk (like, as an example, a bunch of bags
of crack cocain and large sums of money in a nearby envelope).  Would
