When you complain, don't expect to find out the result of your
complaint. It is illegal for U.S. schools to discuss disciplinary
actions with outsiders. The law, the FERPA, applies to all state
school and any private schools that accept federal funds (e.g.
virtually all private universities).

Also, don't expect the person to be punished summarily. Public schools
have a constitutional and (usually) contractual obligation to give
their students due process. Private schools (usually) have a similar
contractional obligation. This is as it should be. If someone posted
something improper so that it looked like it came from you, would you
like to be expelled from the computer with no chance of a hearing and
no opportunity for appeal?

- Carl

