Ah, but then you'll have someone complaining about why they were selected
for the search!  

This can be a real legal issue.  In fact, the US military is prohibited 
from testing individuals for drugs (urine test) on mere suspicion; they 
can only select individuals at random for testing.  

I used this experience (I'm a veteran) in the design of this idea.  The
way I see it, I have three choices:

	- Search on suspicion (I immediately discarded this option),
	- Search everyone on a semi-regular basis, or
	- Search random groups.

Perhaps it would be better to take a random approach; it may even in-
crease the efficiency of the process.  What if, instead of searching
all users' files, we only searched the files of a random 5% of the users
each time?

--Wes

