Let me start out by saying that I am not in favor of censureship

Controlling what is posted from a company or university site
is not exactly the same as censuring in the normal sense.

Why? Because the post is being made with other people's equipment.
In the case of a university it is almost certainly being made on equipment
and a network at least partially supported with government grant money.

Some of these grants are quite clear about what is and what isn't correct
use of these resources.  Often what are considered frivolous, commercial
or illegal use can get everyone in trouble if the university isn't seen
to do something to prove that they are trying to control such uses.

In the case of a company its the same kind of thing. The company
can find itself with angry customers or even legal problems
if they are seen to do nothing in the face of employees using their
equipment and their network access to post or access the network for
purposes which are offensive or illegal.

The fact is that if you want to have totally independent access
all you need to do is subscribe your self to one of many services
that will sell you net access. Even they will take steps if one
of their customers is doing something that will get them in trouble.

But  as you are the customer you are on stronger ground.

Most companies and schools are giving their students and employees
net access for some useful (to them) purpose. The access to news
and mail for other purposes is something of a bonus.

If they want to withdraw that because you are using that access and
their equipment to do things that give them headaches its hard to
see that you have much ground to fight on.

Many companies either don't have net access or control who gets
it for some of those reasons. Universities until fairly recently limited
net access to PHD students and Faculty.  Now that net access is much more
wide spread and many universities have had problems with naive users
who haven't quite realized the tremendous distribution of the net
its hard to blame them for trying to do something about it.
